# Python 3.9 dev/test tooling for the ci.yml python job. Locked separately
# because a resolution for 3.9 is not the same as one for 3.13, and the wheels
# have to exist for the interpreter that installs them.
# Locked output: ci-dev-py39.txt. Refresh via scripts/update-lockfiles.sh.
maturin
# Held at 8.4.2 by the interpreter, not by choice: pytest 9.x requires Python
# 3.10 or newer, and this row exists to test the 3.9 floor that the abi3-py39
# wheel supports. That leaves it below the fix for GHSA-6w46-j5rx-g56g
# (vulnerable tmpdir handling, fixed in 9.0.3), which has no 8.x backport.
#
# Accepted rather than fixable. The advisory needs a second local user on the
# same machine to exploit the temp directory pytest creates; this runs only on
# ephemeral single-tenant CI runners, is dev tooling that ships in no package,
# and is reachable by nothing but the job itself. It goes away when the 3.9 row
# does -- which is a support decision, not a security one.
pytest
